Is white gold or platinum better for a solitaire? Both give a bright, white finish. White gold is lighter on the hand and more affordable per gram, while platinum is denser and naturally hypoallergenic. For most solitaire buyers, 14KT or 18KT white gold delivers a near-identical look at a meaningfully lower cost. Does a white gold solitaire need re-plating over time? White gold jewellery is typically finished with a thin rhodium plating for extra shine. With regular wear, a re-plate every 12 to 18 months keeps the finish bright, though the gold underneath does not wear out. What carat size is standard for a solitaire white gold ring? Most solitaire engagement rings on Lucira range between 0.30 ct and 2 ct, with 0.75 ct to 1.5 ct the most searched sizes in white gold settings. Are Lucira's solitaire diamonds natural or lab-grown? Every solitaire in this collection is set with a certified lab-grown diamond, chemically and optically identical to a natural diamond, with IGI certification included on purchase. Can I exchange a solitaire white gold ring if the size does not fit? Yes. Every purchase is covered under Lucira's lifetime exchange or buyback policy and a 15-day money-back guarantee, in addition to standard resizing support. Explore More Browse the wider Solitaire collection, shop Solitaire Engagement Rings, or see the full Rings range. Building a matching set? Explore Solitaire Pendants and Solitaire Earrings, also available in white gold. Still deciding on a style? Read our guide to engagement ring styles in India.
